.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# **The symlinks into ../wiggles are gone** (2026-08-16). The compendium,
# SPEC.md, PUBLICATION-GATE.md, REPOSITORIES.md and MOVING.md used to be
# symlinked in from the private `wiggles` repo and ignored here by name. They
# now live in `private/`, which is ignored wholesale further down, so the
# per-name rules that used to sit here are gone with them. `chemrich/wiggles` is
# a frozen archive.
#
# Nothing about the gate changed: `PUBLICATION-GATE.md` still holds ten open
# items, the compendium's load-bearing findings still rest on preprints, and
# publishing them under this repo's name would still turn each into a citable
# public assertion. What changed is only *where* the unpublished material sits.
#
# **No trailing slashes anywhere in this file, deliberately.** A trailing slash
# matches a directory and *not* a symlink to one, which is exactly how protean
# came to commit `viewer/node_modules` as a mode-120000 link past a
# `viewer/node_modules/` rule.

# The plan and method documents now live *here* rather than being symlinked in
# — see docs/plans/HANDOFF.md. So `docs/plans` can no longer be ignored
# wholesale, and the rule is **deny-by-default with an allow-list**, never the
# reverse.
#
# That direction is load-bearing and was nearly learned the expensive way. This
# directory is a drop point: the conversation working in protean left a handover
# file here on 2026-08-14 whose own second paragraph read "this lives in
# docs/plans/, which wiggles-em gitignores, so nothing here can reach the public
# repo by accident" — written hours before that stopped being true. Under a
# name-the-private-ones rule it would have been published by the next `git add
# -A`. Under this rule a new file is ignored until someone adds a line below,
# which is a deliberate act.
#
# The four that used to be symlinked here from ../wiggles (SPEC,
# PUBLICATION-GATE, REPOSITORIES, MOVING) are no longer in this directory at
# all — they moved to `private/` on 2026-08-16.
docs/plans/*
!docs/plans/SPLIT.md
!docs/plans/PROTEAN-INTEGRATION.md
!docs/plans/HANDOFF.md
!docs/plans/GUIDELINES.md
!docs/plans/FIX-PLAN.md
!docs/plans/M5-RESULTS.md
!docs/plans/REVIEW-2026-08-13.md

# Unpublished material: the compendium, SPEC.md, the publication gate and its
# tools, and working notes. See private/README.md.
#
# **Ignored wholesale, with no allow-list, and it must stay that way.** The
# `docs/plans` rule above is deny-by-default *because* that directory holds
# tracked public documents and so cannot be ignored outright. This one holds
# nothing public by definition, which makes the stronger rule available — and
# the stronger rule is the one that cannot be got wrong. Anything in here that
# turns out to be publishable gets **moved out**, never allow-listed back in,
# because an allow-list is where the near-miss on 2026-08-14 came from.
#
# This rule is load-bearing in a way the others are not: `private/` holds the
# whole gated compendium, so without this line a single `git add -A` publishes
# ten open gate items. That is not hypothetical — on 2026-08-16 the compendium
# was moved in while this rule sat on an unmerged branch, and `git add -A
# --dry-run` duly offered to stage all nineteen entries.
private
